---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Takeout Fix – Fix Your Google Takeout Photos & Restore Metadata | TakeoutFix"
  description="Looking for a takeout fix for missing photo dates and GPS? TakeoutFix is the fastest take out fix tool to restore EXIF metadata from Google Takeout exports. Works 100% locally in your browser."
>
  <div class="bg-black text-zinc-100 min-h-screen py-24 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative overflow-hidden font-sans">

    <!-- Background glows -->
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/4 w-[500px] h-[500px] bg-indigo-900/10 blur-[150px] rounded-full pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="absolute bottom-20 right-1/4 w-[600px] h-[600px] bg-purple-900/10 blur-[150px] rounded-full pointer-events-none"></div>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center mb-20 relative z-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-800 text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-400 mb-6 font-mono">
        🛠️ Free Takeout Fix Tool · No Install · No Upload
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
        The Ultimate <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-400 via-purple-400 to-pink-500">Takeout Fix</span> for Google Photos
      </h1>

      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-zinc-400 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-8">
        After downloading your photos via Google Takeout, dates go wrong, GPS is missing, and timelines break. 
        TakeoutFix is the #1 <strong class="text-white">take out fix</strong> tool that restores all your missing EXIF metadata instantly — entirely in your browser.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center mb-12">
        <a href="/tool">
          <button id="takeout-fix-cta-primary" class="glass-capsule interactive px-10 h-14 font-semibold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            Fix My Takeout Now →
          </button>
        </a>
        <a href="/restore-data">
          <button id="takeout-fix-cta-guide" class="glass-capsule interactive px-8 h-14 font-semibold text-zinc-300 hover:text-white">
            See How It Works
          </button>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What is a Takeout Fix? -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-20 relative z-10">
      <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">What is a "Takeout Fix" or "Take Out Fix"?</h2>
        <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          When you export your Google Photos library using <strong class="text-zinc-200">Google Takeout</strong>, your photos and videos are downloaded as-is — but all the critical metadata (date taken, GPS location, camera model) is <em>stripped from the file</em> and stored separately in <code class="text-indigo-400">.json</code> sidecar files.
        </p>
        <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          When you import those photos into a new app (Apple Photos, Windows, Google Photos again, Synology, etc.), they show up with <strong class="text-red-400">wrong dates</strong> — usually today's date — and <strong class="text-red-400">no GPS location</strong>. Your 2014 vacation photos appear as if taken today.
        </p>
        <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          A <strong class="text-white">takeout fix</strong> or <strong class="text-white">take out fix</strong> is the process of reuniting those photos with their JSON sidecars and writing the metadata back into the actual image files. TakeoutFix does this automatically — for thousands of files — in seconds.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How It Works -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-20 relative z-10">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white text-center mb-10">How TakeoutFix Performs the Take Out Fix</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6 text-left relative overflow-hidden">
          <span class="absolute right-4 top-2 text-5xl font-extrabold text-white/5 font-mono select-none">1</span>
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/20 flex items-center justify-center mb-3 text-indigo-400 text-lg">📁</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Select Takeout Folder</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
            Open TakeoutFix and select your Google Takeout folder. The engine recursively scans all your .jpg, .mp4, .png files and the corresponding .json sidecars.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6 text-left relative overflow-hidden">
          <span class="absolute right-4 top-2 text-5xl font-extrabold text-white/5 font-mono select-none">2</span>
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-purple-500/10 border border-purple-500/20 flex items-center justify-center mb-3 text-purple-400 text-lg">🔗</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Match & Merge</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
            The fuzzy matching engine handles truncated filenames, edited copies, and Google's naming quirks to correctly pair every photo with its JSON metadata.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6 text-left relative overflow-hidden">
          <span class="absolute right-4 top-2 text-5xl font-extrabold text-white/5 font-mono select-none">3</span>
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-pink-500/10 border border-pink-500/20 flex items-center justify-center mb-3 text-pink-400 text-lg">✅</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">EXIF Restored</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
            Date taken, GPS coordinates, and camera info are injected directly into the image binary — no quality loss, no recompression. Your photos are fully fixed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Who Needs a Takeout Fix? -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-20 relative z-10">
      <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6">Who Needs a Take Out Fix?</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-indigo-400 mt-0.5">→</span>
            <span>Anyone who downloaded photos from <strong class="text-white">Google Takeout</strong> and noticed all photos show today's date</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-indigo-400 mt-0.5">→</span>
            <span>Users migrating from <strong class="text-white">Google Photos to Apple Photos</strong>, Windows Photos, or Synology</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-indigo-400 mt-0.5">→</span>
            <span>People who exported their <strong class="text-white">Google Photos library</strong> and want their memories sorted by actual date</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-indigo-400 mt-0.5">→</span>
            <span>Users with <strong class="text-white">missing GPS locations</strong> on photos after Google Takeout export</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-indigo-400 mt-0.5">→</span>
            <span>Anyone who needs to <strong class="text-white">merge Google Takeout JSON sidecars</strong> back into their photos</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-20 relative z-10 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white text-center mb-8">Takeout Fix — Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">Is TakeoutFix really free?</h3>
        <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. TakeoutFix is free to use for a set of files per session. For unlimited files and batch processing, upgrade to Pro or Super tier. The core takeout fix functionality is free.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">Does the take out fix tool upload my photos?</h3>
        <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">No. TakeoutFix runs 100% in your browser using the HTML5 File System Access API. Your photos never leave your device. There are zero server uploads.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">How is this different from ExifTool or other tools?</h3>
        <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">ExifTool is a powerful command-line tool but requires installation and technical knowledge. TakeoutFix is a browser-based takeout fix that works without installing anything — just open the page and select your folder.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h3 class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">What file types does the take out fix support?</h3>
        <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">TakeoutFix supports JPEG, JPG, PNG, MP4, MOV, and other common photo and video formats exported by Google Takeout.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-20 relative z-10">
      <div class="bg-zinc-950/40 border border-white/5 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-6">Related Guides</h2>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <a href="/restore-data" class="block p-4 bg-zinc-900/50 rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 hover:border-indigo-500/30 transition-colors">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200 mb-1">Restore Data Guide</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Complete walkthrough for restoring all metadata</div>
          </a>
          <a href="/metadata-fixer" class="block p-4 bg-zinc-900/50 rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 hover:border-indigo-500/30 transition-colors">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200 mb-1">Metadata Fixer</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Online EXIF metadata repair tool</div>
          </a>
          <a href="/google-photos-metadata-fix" class="block p-4 bg-zinc-900/50 rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 hover:border-indigo-500/30 transition-colors">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200 mb-1">Google Photos Metadata Fix</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Fix missing dates & GPS from Google Photos</div>
          </a>
          <a href="/fix-google-takeout-dates" class="block p-4 bg-zinc-900/50 rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 hover:border-indigo-500/30 transition-colors">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200 mb-1">Fix Takeout Dates</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Restore original timestamps to photos</div>
          </a>
          <a href="/google-takeout-to-apple-photos" class="block p-4 bg-zinc-900/50 rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 hover:border-indigo-500/30 transition-colors">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200 mb-1">Takeout → Apple Photos</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Migrate Google Takeout to Apple Photos</div>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center py-16 border-t border-zinc-900 relative z-10">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4 text-white">Start Your Takeout Fix Now</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 mb-8 max-w-md mx-auto">
        Fix missing metadata from your Google Takeout photos in minutes. Free, private, and instant.
      </p>
      <a href="/tool">
        <button id="takeout-fix-cta-bottom" class="glass-capsule interactive px-12 h-14 font-semibold text-white">
          Open TakeoutFix →
        </button>
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- JSON-LD for this page -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is a takeout fix?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "A takeout fix is the process of restoring missing EXIF metadata (dates, GPS, camera info) to photos downloaded via Google Takeout. TakeoutFix automates this process in your browser."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is TakeoutFix free?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. TakeoutFix offers a free tier. The core takeout fix functionality is available at no cost."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Does the takeout fix upload my photos?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "No. TakeoutFix runs 100% locally in your browser. Your photos never leave your device."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>
</Layout>
